    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="1018" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg922"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to the Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Telegram concerning difficult ies of commissioners at Habana received. Our
                    commissioners seem to have made mistake in discussing or answering any question
                    as to Spain’s relinquishment of sovereignty over and title to Cuba. Their duties
                    relate solely to that practical military operation of immediate evacuation. It
                    seems to us they should have said this, instead of accepting an issue as to the
                    time when Spanish sovereignty will be relinquished. Not of vital importance when
                    Spain formally relinquishes her sovereignty, or whether she ever formally
                    relinquishes it, if we are in possession. This was specific purpose of article 4
                    of protocol.</p>
                <p>We meet Spanish Commissioners this afternoon and shall go forward with articles
                    as to Cuba, Porto Rico, and Guam, without mentioning questions before
                    commissioners at Habana.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
